{
  "about": [
    "The kit's class names (docs/plans/2026-09-28-the-interface-kit-and-its-looks.md, §3.4 and decision 4): the house's own, with no prefix, so a page that draws one keeps its class.",
    "Started with the families §3.4 lists, as components.css and record.css name them on 28 September 2026: .btn*, .pill*, .chip*, .tally*, .mark, .avatar*, .empty*, .more-*, .confirm*, .field-error*, .pp-toast*, .ui-tip, .stabs* and the record kit's .rec-*. Their rules move into kit.css with step 2.1; a new primitive's name joins with its rules.",
    "The measures read this list (tooling/scripts/tests/_css.mjs): a name here is a primitive in any stylesheet but kit.css. Every name is one a stylesheet of the dashboard names, and a primitive by its words or declared in kit.css; every class kit.css declares is here (tests/styles/kit-css.test.mjs).",
    "Modifiers are the other classes kit.css names, which draw nothing of their own: a primitive's state or variant written as a word of its own (.btn.danger, .ui-tip.show, .stabs-tab.active, .more-menu.align-right, .escape, .placed, .up), and what another part of the house draws inside one (the Icon's .icon, a key's .kbd, a hand-drawn .dot). A page's .active or .danger is its own, so the measures read the classes alone, and a modifier is a class kit.css declares and no primitive by its words (tests/styles/kit-css.test.mjs)."
  ],
